# Paths deliberately kept out of BOTH lanes — the machine-readable half of
# ~/.config/CLAUDE.md → "Deliberately not tracked (audited)", which keeps the
# reasoning in prose. assay's yadm-coverage station reads this file; anything under a
# scanned root that is neither tracked, nor matched by yadm/encrypt, nor inside
# a pruned runtime directory, nor listed here is reported as undecided.
#
# Format: <path-or-glob><TAB><reason>. Globs are $HOME-relative, `*` does not
# cross `/`, `**` does. `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# The point is that each judgment is made ONCE and recorded. A line here is a
# decision, not a mute button — write the reason as if the next reader has no
# memory of this one, because they do not.
#
# Same obfuscation convention as yadm/encrypt: no entry, and no reason text,
# may name a private organization or identity.

# --- Credentials: live, revocable, never in a repo ------------------------
.npmrc	registry auth tokens; re-issued by npm login
.sentryclirc	auth token for an error tracker; re-issued from its web UI
.config/slack-mcp/*	session tokens for a workspace, plus the wrapper that loads them
.config/intelephense/global/*	licence key, and an activation cache whose filename embeds it
.config/gh/hosts.yml	`gh auth login` writes an oauth token here
.config/gh-benefactor/*	second gh profile; same reason, seeded by snippets/shared/15-gh-benefactor.sh
.ssh/known_hosts*	host fingerprints this machine has accepted

# --- Regenerated by bootstrap or by the tool itself ------------------------
.config/yadm/config	rewritten by snippets/shared/02-gpg.sh; hardcodes $HOME, so the identity guard bars it
.tilde-switch	written by snippets/macos/20-tilde-switch.sh
.config/pluma/config.toml	an all-commented template; its relic writes a fresh one
.config/op/config	device registration, written by the tool
.config/jgit/config	filesystem timings an IDE measured on this disk
.config/composer/*	public keys and an .htaccess, installed by composer
.config/asciinema/install-id	per-install identifier
.config/cagent/.cagent_first_run	first-run marker
.config/configstore/**	update-notifier state for npm packages

# --- Managed by another manifest that IS tracked ---------------------------
.config/fish/functions/*	fisher plugins; restored from the tracked fish_plugins
.config/fish/conf.d/fzf.fish	same
.config/fish/conf.d/sdk.fish	same
.config/fish/completions/fisher.fish	same
.config/fish/completions/fzf_configure_bindings.fish	same
.config/fish/completions/sdk.fish	same
.config/fish/completions/docker.fish	symlink into a container app bundle
.config/fish/completions/kubectl.fish	symlink into a container app bundle
.config/fish/completions/orbctl.fish	symlink into a container app bundle
.local/bin/*	the externally-managed PATH lane; see .local/bin/.reliquary-managed
.local/bin/.reliquary-managed	the registry for that lane, written by reliquary/lib/install-on-path.sh

# --- Machine-local state and caches ----------------------------------------
.bash_history	shell history
.zsh_history	shell history
.viminfo	editor state
.lesshst	pager history
.mysql_history	client history
.CFUserTextEncoding	macOS per-user locale marker
.claude.json	agent state, including per-project history
.claude.json.backup	the agent's own rolling backup of the above
.claude/.last-cleanup	agent housekeeping marker
.claude/.last-update-result.json	agent housekeeping marker
.claude/daemon.log	agent log
.claude/history.jsonl	agent prompt history
.config/fish/fish_variables	fish universal variables, written by the shell
.config/zsh/.zcompdump	completion cache, rebuilt by compinit
.config/zsh/.zsh_sessions/*	per-session shell state, written by zsh
